    "body": "2026 SEMA Show • Ford Frostwarden, a Bronco SUV With Over 1,200 HP, the R125 and F-250 Also in Tow\nVolkswagen Puts a Price Tag on the 2027 California, Here’s How Much the Campervan Costs\n7 photos\nPhoto: Volkswagen\nHaving been unveiled earlier this year, when summer just kicked off in the northern hemisphere, the 2027 Volkswagen California is now available to order in the United Kingdom.\nThe tiny home on wheels is a 2026 model in continental Europe, but it is marketed as a 2027 model in the UK because while the order books have officially opened, the deliveries will commence early next year.\nMind you, the visual updates are not that dramatic to make you mistake it for an all-new ride, but they will definitely make it more noticeable. The biggest novelties revolve around the model’s front fascia, where it features a revised lighting signature, different headlights, and a new bumper that looks a lot cleaner this time around. And the headlights also shine brighter, according to the German car manufacturer.\nThe changes continue on the inside, where the latest iteration of the Volkswagen California benefits from a new dashboard panel that comprises a bigger 12.9-inch infotainment system with a free-standing display and a tablet-like design. There is also an upgraded digital gauge cluster, and the improved materials and decorative stitching are also part of the refresh.\nPhoto: Volkswagen Volkswagen also mentions the power latching sliding doors and tailgate, as well as the new wheel designs, which range from 17 to 19 inches in diameter. A new electric stationary air conditioning system is also on deck, albeit on the eHybrid 4Motion model, which allows the campervan to be cooled, ventilated, and heated while it is charging for up to eight hours, and this makes it ideal for sleeping in comfort regardless of the outside weather.\nThe color palette has also been updated and now includes the Reed Green, Grey Brown, Grenadilla Black, and Sunset Red. All of these are metallic, and they are joined by the two-tone Grenadilla Black / Sunset Red, and Candy White / Grey Brown. The model can be specified in one of the 19 solid, two-tone, and metallic colors available, in addition to a black roof design, which is optional.\nThe latest generation of the Travel Assist system is on deck, and enables assisted lane changing on motorways on the 2027 Volkswagen California. Moreover, traffic light recognition is also on deck in a premiere. Integrated Emergency Assist is also included, guiding the vehicle to the hard shoulder or the outermost lane in case the driver suffers a medical emergency, and numerous other safety gizmos are also included.\nBut what about the pricing, you ask? Well, the most affordable version of the 2027 Volkswagen California in the United Kingdom is the Beach, equipped with a 2-liter TDI diesel engine. The mill is rated at 150 ps (148 hp/110 kW), and drives the front wheels through a seven-speed DSG automatic transmission. Pricing starts at 66,334 pounds (equal to $88,970), and it includes VAT and OTR costs.\nVolkswagen’s 2027 California Beach is also available with the 1.5 eHybrid powertrain, which offers 245 ps (242 hp/180 kW), utilizes a six-speed DSG automatic transmission, and features 4Motion all-wheel drive. In this case, customers must fork out a minimum of 74,637 pounds ($100,110).\nThe Coast is next in line, and just like the lesser Beach variant, it utilizes the same powertrains . Pricing for the diesel-powered variant starts at 71,464 pounds ($95,855), and the electrified model is available from 79,672 pounds ($106,862).\nPhoto: Volkswagen Last but not least, the Ocean is the top trim level of the 2027 Volkswagen California in the UK. The diesel variant kicks off at 79,762 pounds ($106,980), and the hybridized one can be yours from a minimum of 87,970 pounds ($117,990).\nVolkswagen’s 2027 California Ocean 150 PS 2.0 TDI 7-speed DSG is available on a 48-month contract with 10,000 miles (~16,000 km) per year with a deposit contribution of 5,000 pounds ($6,705), a customer deposit of 16,511.82 pounds ($22,147), and 47 monthly payments of 549 pounds ($736). The optional final payment is 44,253 pounds ($59,355).\nThe latest iteration of the camper van benefits from the company’s enhanced warranty and service plan, the 5+ Promise at no extra cost, which includes five services, three for electric models, three MOTs, and a five-year warranty and five years of roadside assistance.\nIn Germany, the VW California campervan in the Beach configuration has a starting price of 66,087 euros, which equals $73,945 at today’s exchange rate.\nAs for the larger and better-equipped Volkswagen Grand California , customers must choose between the 600, 680, Dune 600, and Dune 680 models. Pricing for the Grand California starts at 84,208 pounds ($112,945) OTR, including VAT for the most affordable version. The 680 model kicks off at 86,986 pounds ($116,670), the Dune 600 at 85,408 pounds ($114,555), and the Dune 680 at 88,186 pounds ($118,280), the brochure, which is available on the company’s official website (Vans) reveals.\nSo, is the 2027 Volkswagen California campervan your next home away from home? Or does the pricier and bigger Grand California sound better?\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nVolkswagen California Volkswagen California 2027 Volkswagen California prices new cars UK camper van\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Cristian Gnaticov\nAfter a series of unfortunate events put an end to Cristian's dream of entering a custom built & tuned old-school Dacia into a rally competition, he moved on to drive press cars and write for a living. He's worked for several automotive online journals and now he's back at autoevolution after his first tour in the mid-2000s. Full profile\nUP NEXT Android Auto Cielo Update Could Include More Surprises, Android Auto 18.1 Code Shows",
